  "document": "Move Over, Darling\nMove Over, Darling is a 1963 American comedy film starring Doris Day, James Garner, and Polly Bergen and directed by Michael Gordon. The picture was a remake of a 1940 screwball comedy film, \"My Favorite Wife\", with Irene Dunne, Cary Grant and Gail Patrick. In between these movies, an unfinished version entitled \"Something's Got to Give\" began shooting in 1962, directed by George Cukor and starring Marilyn Monroe (she got fired but hired again and died soon after) and Dean Martin."
